      <h1>How to Read <em>Normal Distribution</em> Probabilities</h1>
      <p class="dek">In a normal distribution, a probability is an area under the bell curve. Once that clicks, every question, the chance of landing below a value, above it, between two, or outside them, becomes a matter of adding or subtracting areas. Here is how to read those areas, the 68-95-99.7 shortcut, and why two calculators can disagree on the same problem.</p>
